The error is caused by the fact that `service.createEncounter(dto)` returns a Promise, but you're trying to use `expect(result).toBeDefined()` which expects a value and not a Promise. 

You should instead wait for the Promise to resolve with `await service.createEncounter(dto)` before checking if it is defined:

javascript
it('should create a new encounter if patient is active and does not have an active encounter', async () => {
    const dto = new CreateEncounterDto();
    dto.patientId = '123';
    jest.spyOn(encounterRepositoryMock, 'findActiveByPatient').mockResolvedValue(null);
    jest.spyOn(patientServiceMock, 'getPatientById').mockResolvedValue({ active: true });
    
    const result = await service.createEncounter(dto);
    expect(result).toBeDefined();
});

This will ensure that the test waits for `service.createEncounter(dto)` to resolve before checking if it is defined.

